==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|obsequii|obsequiī|complaisant, yielding|lang=la}}, alteration of {{term|obsequia||compliance|lang=la}} (by confusion, in association with {{term|exequiae|exsequia|funeral rites|lang=la}}, from {{term|exsequi|exsequī|follow or accompany to the grave|lang=la}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK|US}} {{IPA|/ˈɔbsɪ.kwiː/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|obsequies}}

# The last [[office]] for the [[dead]]
# {{context|chiefly|in the plural|lang=en}} A [[funeral]] [[rite]] or [[service]].
#* '''1919 ''' — [[w:Ronald Firbank|Ronald Firbank]], ''[[w:Valmouth|Valmouth]]'', Duckworth, hardback edition, page 13 
#*: But, to-day, there were no '''obsequies''' to observe at all.

====Usage notes====
* in modern usage, it is mainly in the plural: "[[obsequies]]", and not to be confused with [[obsequious]]

